    "body": "## Summary\n\n- reject missing or transient principals before account/profile/password persistence access\n- enforce persisted identities before job creation, private job lists, recommendations and publication recovery\n- fail closed before attachment visibility/storage and wallet-history repository access\n- add regression coverage proving rejected principals cannot reach repositories or providers\n- update the security contract and the 965-point roadmap\n\n## Scope\n\n- 1 commit\n- 14 files\n- +210 / -7\n- base: `2e854b3314c3005213f416374cda75d2b9a4d57e`\n- head: `db132d50fb3fb3c8e3a7e6e3493bf7a2062ce0bf`\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- local and remote tree SHA match: `65661cabfc9647a06424f602f8fa0dac3a5ba2d2`\n- first CI run exposed an incorrect expected exception in the new regression test; the test now follows the existing neutral `ResourceNotFoundException` contract\n- merge only after all workflows for the exact current head SHA are green and review threads are clear",
